.\" jailrun man page
.\"
.\" To view:   man ./man/man1/jailrun.1
.\" To install: cp man/man1/jailrun.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.\"
.Dd July 24, 2026
.Dt JAILRUN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailrun
.Nd native-first OCI runtime for FreeBSD jails
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Cm COMMAND
.Op Ar args Ns ...
.Pp
.Nm run
.Op Fl -rm
.Op Fl v Ar HOST:CTR Ns Op :ro
.Op Fl e Ar KEY=VALUE
.Op Fl w Ar DIR
.Op Fl -timeout Ar SECONDS
.Op Fl -network Ar NETWORK
.Op Fl -allow-raw-sockets
.Op Fl -no-rctl
.Op Fl -allow-unrestricted-devfs
.Op Fl -rctl-rule Ar ACTION:VALUE
.Op Fl it
.Ar IMAGE
.Op Ar CMD Op Ar ARGS Ns ...
.Pp
.Nm exec
.Op Fl e Ar KEY=VALUE
.Op Fl w Ar DIR
.Op Fl -timeout Ar SECONDS
.Ar JAIL_NAME
.Ar CMD
.Op Ar ARGS Ns ...
.Pp
.Nm pull
.Op Fl -authfile Ar PATH
.Op Fl -creds Ar USER:PASS
.Ar IMAGE
.Pp
.Nm ps
.Op Fl a
.Pp
.Nm logs
.Ar JAIL_NAME
.Pp
.Nm explain
.Op Fl -manifest Ar FILE
.Op Fl -format Brq text | json
.Op Ar IMAGE
.Pp
.Nm scan
.Op Fl -format Brq text | json
.Ar IMAGE
.Op Ar IMAGE ...\&
.Pp
.Nm doctor
.Op Fl -format Brq text | json
.Pp
.Nm gc
.Op Fl -fix
.Op Fl -format Brq text | json
.Pp
.Nm version
.Pp
.Nm freeze
.Ar JAIL_NAME
.Pp
.Nm thaw
.Ar JAIL_NAME
.Pp
.Nm hibernate
.Ar JAIL_NAME
.Pp
.Nm restore
.Ar JAIL_NAME
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs Linux and FreeBSD OCI images inside FreeBSD jails.
It resolves an image reference via
.Xr skopeo 1 ,
unpacks the OCI layers into a ZFS dataset, probes every ELF binary to
determine whether a native FreeBSD substitute exists, and creates a
jail with the image rootfs as its filesystem.
.Pp
Binaries for which a native FreeBSD substitute is known (e.g.,
.Nm python3 ,
.Nm bash ,
.Nm git )
are shadowed with the native version via the bakery system.
All other Linux binaries run transparently through the Linuxulator
(FreeBSD's Linux ABI compatibility layer).
.Pp
The default network mode is
.Sq none
\(em the jail has no connectivity.
Use
.Fl network Ns = Ns Ar allow Ns Li = Ns Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar port
for destination-scoped egress.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "explain"
.It Cm run
Run a command in a new jail container from an OCI image.
Flags mirror
.Xr docker 1 Ns 's
.Fl rm ,
.Fl v ,
.Fl e ,
.Fl w ,
and
.Fl it .
.Pp
.Fl -timeout
limits wall-clock execution time.
.Pp
.Fl -network
controls network access:
.Sq none ,
.Sq inherit ,
or
.Sq allow= Ns Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar port Ns Op ,... .
.Pp
.Fl -rctl-rule
applies a FreeBSD rctl resource limit
.Pq e.g. Ic maxproc:deny=100 .
.Pp
.Fl -allow-unrestricted-devfs
relaxes the default restrictive
.Xr devfs 8
ruleset (needed for some toolchains that access
.Pa /dev/random
or
.Pa /dev/tap ) .
.It Cm exec
Run an additional command inside an already-running jail
(similar to
.Ic docker exec ) .
Non-interactive only (no PTY).
.It Cm pull
Resolve and unpack an image into the local store cache
without creating a jail.
Useful to pre-warm a batch of images ahead of time.
.It Cm ps
List jailrun-managed runs from the run-state database.
.Fl a
shows exited/killed history in addition to running jails.
.It Cm logs
Print a run's captured stdout/stderr from the run-state database.
The jail must be named as shown by
.Ic jailrun ps .
.It Cm explain
Answer \(lqwill this image run under jailrun, how, and what would make it
better\(rq by rendering the substitution manifest.
Supports
.Fl -manifest Ar FILE
to load a pre-produced manifest from disk (works on any host),
or
.Ar IMAGE
to resolve it the same way
.Ic jailrun run
does (FreeBSD host only).
Output format:
.Sq text
(default) or
.Sq json .
.It Cm scan
Run probe() against one or more images and report an aggregate
native-vs-linuxulator summary across the batch.
FreeBSD host only.
.It Cm doctor
Inspect the host system and report jailrun readiness: required tools
.Pq Xr skopeo 1 , Xr bsdtar 1 ,
kernel modules
.Pq Xr linux 4 ,
ZFS pool existence, and pkg trust key setup.
Prints the exact fix command for each failing check.
.It Cm gc
Find and clean up orphaned jails, ZFS datasets, and
run-state database rows left behind after an unclean shutdown.
Default: dry-run only.
.Fl -fix
applies the cleanup actions.
.It Cm version
Print the jailrun version (git describe), FreeBSD release, and
Python version.
.It Cm freeze , thaw , hibernate , restore
Lifecycle operations delegated to
.Nm bsdos_lifecycled .
.Ic freeze
SIGSTOPs a jail's processes (0% CPU, state retained in RAM).
.Ic thaw
SIGCONTs a frozen jail.
.Ic hibernate
ZFS-snapshots the jail's rootfs then SIGSTOPs (RAM-light).
.Ic restore
reverts a hibernated or frozen jail to running state.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /var/jailrun/images/" -compact
.It Pa /var/jailrun/images/
Unpacked OCI image rootfs datasets
.Pq ZFS datasets: Cm jailrun/images/ Ns Ar image_id
.It Pa /var/jailrun/bases/
Native-substitution base datasets
.Pq Cm jailrun/bases/
.It Pa /var/cache/jailrun/oci/
OCI image layout cache
.Pq Xr skopeo 1
.It Pa /var/cache/jailrun/manifests/
Pre-computed substitution manifests
.Pq keyed by image_id
.It Pa /var/db/jailrun/
Run-state SQLite database + per-run log files
.It Pa /var/log/jailrun/
Runtime log output
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "JAILRUN_REGISTRY_AUTHFILE"
.It Ev JAILRUN_EXTRACT_IN_JAIL
When set to
.Sq 1 ,
OCI layer extraction runs inside a throwaway jail
(slower but isolates the tar parser from the host).
.It Ev JAILRUN_REGISTRY_AUTHFILE
Path to a skopeo-compatible registry auth file
(default: not set; anonymous pull).
.It Ev JAILRUN_STORE_BACKEND
Storage backend:
.Sq zfs
(default, requires ZFS) or
.Sq plaindir
(flat directory, for testing).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ jailrun run --rm alpine:latest sh -c 'echo hello from alpine'
$ jailrun run --rm --network allow=pypi.org:443 ubuntu:24.04 pip install torch
$ jailrun pull debian:stable-slim
$ jailrun explain debian:stable-slim --format json
$ jailrun doctor
$ jailrun gc --fix
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr skopeo 1 ,
.Xr linux 4 ,
.Xr devfs 8 ,
.Xr rctl 8
